From: JetHub HAOS port <dev@jethome.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: drop forced -Werror for CONFIG_AMLOGIC_DRIVER builds

The vendor tree appends -Werror unconditionally whenever
CONFIG_AMLOGIC_DRIVER=y. That is independent of CONFIG_WERROR, so the
usual "# CONFIG_WERROR is not set" has no effect here.

HAOS enables subsystems this vendor tree was never compiled with
(AppArmor, EROFS, additional netfilter and USB-serial drivers) and
builds with a newer toolchain than the vendor used, so warnings that
were never triggered upstream become hard errors and stop the build.

Drop the forced -Werror; warnings remain visible, they just no longer
abort the build.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -706,7 +706,6 @@
 LINUXINCLUDE   += \
 		-I$(srctree)/$(COMMON_DRIVERS_DIR)/include \
 		-I$(srctree)/$(COMMON_DRIVERS_DIR)/include/uapi
-KBUILD_CFLAGS += -Werror
 KBUILD_AFLAGS += -Wno-unused-command-line-argument
 endif
 
